You are an adversarial reviewer of scientific figures for a research proposal. The attached PNGs are rendered at 2x from SVG and will be displayed about 850 px wide. Try hard to find reasons each figure should not ship. For EACH image, by file order, report: (a) overlapping or colliding text, (b) lines or arrows that cross text or other arrows confusingly, (c) arrows whose direction or endpoints are ambiguous, (d) text too small to read at display size, (e) excess text that belongs in a caption, (f) the one main point and whether a reader gets it in 5 seconds, (g) concrete fixes with coordinates or element names. Then give a verdict per figure: ship / fix / redraw. Focus: Proposal 08, seven figures in this order. (1) one-video-two-referrals: the same clip under two referral lines follows two defensible paths to a shorter or longer hold time (illustrative). (2) better-measurer-worse-decision: shrinking toward the referral lowers MSE while the blind-calibrated decision penalty rises from zero; the diamond is the Bayes report gamma_B (computed in simulation). (3) calibration-bug-or-information-bug: a one-to-one shift can be recalibrated away, while a cap under the high-risk referral maps different blind values to one report (schematic); below the cap the two referral lines coincide on purpose. (4) path-splicing-factorial: crossing path referral with report referral gives a two-by-two factorial with direct (rightward) and indirect (downward) effects. (5) blind-analysis-harness: measure blind, commit, then reveal the referral to interpretation; the decision uses the referral once as the prior. (6) self-improvement-design: three optimizers by three rewards with 8, 3 and 4 seeds, six checkpoints per run audited on sealed people. (7) predicted-routes-by-optimizer: hypothetical prediction that both optimizer types reach the gamma_B band in total effect but only GEPA and ACE put most of it through the path.. Do not run commands or modify files.

